<title>UK: CRICKET-NATWEST TROPHY QUARTER-FINAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-NATWEST TROPHY QUARTER-FINAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of NatWest Trophy (60</p>
<p>overs) quarter-finals on Tuesday:</p>
<p>At Derby: Sussex beat Derbyshire by five wickets. Derbyshire</p>
<p>327-8 innings closed (C.Adams 129 not out; V.Drakes 4-62).</p>
<p>Sussex 329-5 in 59.2 overs (R.Rao 158).</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Glamorgan beat Yorkshire by one wicket.</p>
<p>Yorkshire 236-8 innings closed (D.Lehmann 105). Glamorgan 237-9</p>
<p>in 59 overs (M.Maynard 62, R.Croft 55; D.Gough 4-36).</p>
<p>At Lord's: Warwickshire beat Middlesex by 28 runs.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 286-6 innings closed (D.Hemp 112, D.Ostler 51).</p>
<p>Middlesex 258-9 innings closed (M.Ramprakash 98, K.Brown 50).</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Essex beat Nottinghamshire by three wickets.</p>
<p>Nottinghamshire 288-5 innings closed (P.Johnson 106, R.Robinson</p>
<p>52). Essex 289-7 in 58.2 overs (N.Hussain 89 not out).</p>
</text>
